A||||4||deceler8||Am I missing something re: A/C Belt ?||||13
Z||000000||deceler8||10-26-1999||05:18 PM||||Who in the hell designed the A/C belt system on this car ('86 2m4, automatic) ?<P>Have been dreading changing belts since I bought the car last month, but getting them off was easy. Alternator belt a snap to replace, but how do you tighten the A/C belt?<P>Don't tell me to order the fanbelt tightener (I just got off the phone with JC Whitney...thanks to whomever posted the item #) as I'll have it in a few days...can I drive with the A/C belt off or can someone please tell me how it's tightened ?<P>Sincerely, <P>The Young and the Beltless||||reg||13
Z||000001||theogre||10-26-1999||06:29 PM||||Dear Beltless,<P>yes you can run without a belt. your pants might fall down, but you can do it. ((No it won't hurt the car any.))<P>you have to losen several bolts on the compressor. You have to do it from under the car. Sorry, ain't no other way.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||10-26-1999||07:59 PM||||The loosening part I got. My question is how do you tighten it ?<P>What do you pry against to rotate the compressor so the belt tightens ?<P>Really, I'm semi-intelligent (dun' grajeeated from the sixth grade), but I don't see where there's anything to pry against.<P>My other cars have had idler brackets to adjust the A/C belt, obviously this one doesn't. ||||reg||8
Z||000003||Linx||10-26-1999||10:02 PM||||Heh heh heh...<P>I did mine from <I>under</I> the car.  Using a big ol' flat blade screw driver between the bracket and the compressor.  Probably the hardest way to do it...<P>But you ordered the tool, so be patient and when it comes, you can stay on top.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||10-29-1999||03:51 PM||||All I can say is the guy who invented the fanbelt tightener gets my vote for the Nobel Prize...makes the A/C belt a 10 minute job.<P>Thanks again (my heartfelt thanks) for the tip.||||reg||6
